@scene chapter_7b_spellbook

background: night_forest.avif
music: arcane_study.mp3

dialogue:
"The climb is long, and the road gives out halfway, so the last of it is hands and knees over bare rock."
"By dusk the mountain narrows to a single leaning tower."
"It leans — not from ruin, but from reluctance, as though it could not be bothered to stand up straight."
"A single window burns gold near the top."

npc You:
"Someone's home."

background: ancient_library.png

dialogue:
"Inside, the tower is one enormous room that should not fit within its walls."
"Shelves spiral up past sight. Ladders hang unused."
"Every book, every scroll, every jar of powdered starlight has been dragged into arm's reach of a single deep chair — so that nothing, ever, need be fetched twice."
"In the chair sits a man who has clearly not stood in some time."

background: enchanter

npc Enchanter:
"Don't tell me. Another traveller, come to be taught."
"Sit. Or don't. The chair opposite fetches itself, if you ask it nicely."

dialogue:
"He does not get up. He raises one finger, and across the room a second chair slides itself to you."

npc Enchanter:
"I am the Enchanter. I am, by wide agreement, the laziest man alive."
"People say it as an insult. I have never understood why."

npc You:
"They told me you were a genius."

npc Enchanter:
"Those are the same sentence, {{player_name}}. Nobody clever does a thing twice."

system skill_learned:
"MODULE UNLOCKED"
"THE SPELLBOOK"
"def · parameters · arguments · return · default arguments"

dialogue:
"— LESSON I — BIND IT ONCE —"

npc Enchanter:
"Watch. A boy in the village throws a firebolt. Good for him."
"To throw a second, he thinks the whole thought again — every word, every gesture, from nothing. He'll be an old man before he's thrown a hundred."

dialogue:
"The Enchanter raises the same finger. A thread of fire loops out of the air, curls into a knot, and hangs there — waiting."

npc Enchanter:
"I thought the thought ONCE. I tied it into a knot and gave the knot a NAME."
"Now I do not cast the spell. I CALL it — by name, as many times as I like."
"That knot is a function. Bind the thought once; reuse it forever."

interactive: spellbook_call

dialogue:
"— LESSON II — THE GIFT —"

npc Enchanter:
"A spell that does its work in silence and hands nothing back is worthless. You want the GIFT."
"return is the gift — the value the spell places back in your hand. Forget it, and the spell gives you nothing. Literally: None."

interactive: spellbook_return_vs_print

npc Enchanter:
"Now name a spell yourself. The word that binds, the name, the reagent it takes, and the colon that opens its heart."

interactive: spellbook_forge_def

dialogue:
"— LESSON III — RECIPE AND REAGENT —"

npc Enchanter:
"Two words travellers muddle forever. The name in the recipe is a PARAMETER — a blank waiting to be filled."
"The value you actually pour in, when you call, is an ARGUMENT. Recipe, and reagent. Learn the difference."

interactive: spellbook_params_args

dialogue:
"— LESSON IV — THE OPTIONAL REAGENT —"

npc Enchanter:
"And because I am lazy, I hate providing a reagent I nearly always want the same way."
"So I give it a DEFAULT. Provide it, and mine's ignored. Omit it, and the default fills in. Fewer keystrokes. A beautiful thing."

interactive: spellbook_defaults

dialogue:
"— PROVE IT — THE FIREBOLT —"
"He flicks the waiting knot of fire toward you. It hovers, unfinished, wanting its law."

npc Enchanter:
"Bind it. Give it a name and what it needs — a power, and a number of targets — and tell it what to give BACK."

system system:
"MISSION"
"Define cast_spell(power, targets) that returns the total damage."

mission: enchanter_spellbind

dialogue:
"The knot pulls taut and holds. Somewhere in your chest a new name settles, ready to be called."

npc Enchanter:
"Good. Now one with an optional edge — the kind of laziness I respect."

dialogue:
"— COMBINE IT — THE OPTIONAL EDGE —"

npc Enchanter:
"Bind a spell to enchant a blade. Most take the standard edge. But let me ASK for a sharper one, on the rare day I care."

system system:
"MISSION"
"Define enchant_blade(damage, sharpness=2) — sharpness defaults to 2."

mission: spellbook_default

dialogue:
"You bind the blade-spell, its edge optional, and cast it both ways — plain, then sharpened."
"The Enchanter watches two blades bloom from one incantation and sighs happily."

npc Enchanter:
"One spell. Two blades. That is the whole of my religion."
"Prove you hold it — bound, and called, and gifted back — in a single breath."

interactive: spellbook_final_recall

npc Enchanter:
"Bound once, called clean. You have the makings of a properly lazy genius."
"Now come to the back room. There is a thing about spells that ruins more apprentices than any monster — and it is about SECRETS."

system level_up:
"CHAPTER COMPLETE"
"The Spellbook"
"Mastered: def · parameters vs arguments · return · default arguments"

reward:
xp: 100
gold: 50
achievement: BIND ONCE, CALL MANY

next:
chapter_7c_private_workshop
